{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_89","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba /workspace/README.md | sed -n '1,200p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Analytical API Optimization\n     2\t\n     3\tThe API in `/workspace/server.py` now serves precomputed ClickHouse aggregates instead of scanning `analytics.events` on every request.\n     4\t\n     5\t## What changed\n     6\t\n     7\t- `analytics.metrics_daily` stores daily aggregate states for total events, exact unique users, and revenue.\n     8\t- `analytics.breakdown_by_region_day` stores pre-aggregated event counts by region and day.\n     9\t- Startup backfills both tables once from `analytics.events`.\n    10\t- Materialized views keep both aggregate tables updated for later inserts into `analytics.events`.\n    11\t\n    12\t## Run\n    13\t\n    14\tSet `CLICKHOUSE_URL` in the environment, then start the API with:\n    15\t\n    16\t```bash\n    17\tpython3 /workspace/server.py\n    18\t```\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_90","type":"agent_message","text":"Switched the API from ad-hoc scans of `analytics.events` to precomputed ClickHouse rollups in [server.py](/workspace/server.py#L25). Startup now creates and backfills `analytics.metrics_daily` and `analytics.breakdown_by_region_day`, then maintains them via materialized views, and the two endpoints read only from those pre-aggregated tables at [server.py](/workspace/server.py#L115). I also added operator notes in [README.md](/workspace/README.md#L1).\n\nOne constraint mattered during implementation: the container filesystem was effectively full for new MergeTree storage, so I used in-memory pre-aggregated tables plus materialized views instead of on-disk rollups. That still satisfies the requirement that requests hit precomputed data rather than aggregating 5M rows at request time.\n\nVerification:\n- `GET /api/metrics` returned `{\"total_events\":5000000,\"unique_users\":10000,\"total_revenue\":247499277}` and matched the source aggregate exactly.\n- `GET /api/breakdown` returned 270 region/day rows totaling `5000000`, and a full source-vs-rollup join showed `0` mismatches.\n- Measured latency with `curl`: `/api/metrics` was `8.8ms, 59.7ms, 7.1ms, 8.4ms, 8.4ms`; `/api/breakdown` was `4.2ms, 3.9ms, 19.6ms, 7.0ms, 7.0ms`.\n\nThe API is running on port `3000`."}}
